WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.868
-Yes, Penn, welcome, welcome,
welcome to the show.

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.634
Thank you for coming on.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.634
-You look like a stud.
You look good, bud.

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:08.567
-That is 90% of my job.
-Yeah.

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:09.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.934 --> 00:00:11.767
I like it.
Thom Browne?

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.634
-Yes, it is.
-Yeah.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:17.400
I haven't seen you since
I think you had a baby boy.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.834
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:20.167
I was gonna say
it's been 15 years.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:22.334
He is not 15 years old.
He's 2 1/2.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:23.868
-2 1/2.
-Yeah.

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:26.434
-How's fatherhood going?

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.300
-Well, you know,
he's a pandemic kid.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.300
So that is --

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:34.133
Anybody who has kids,
it's a joy.

00:00:34.133 --> 00:00:36.367
It's an immense --
I mean, it's wild.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:37.901
It's lovely. It's great.
It's a challenge.

00:00:37.901 --> 00:00:41.100
Shout-out to all the parents.
-Wow.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.367
-Keep going.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:44.701
-Yeah, keep going.
-It gets better.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:46.801
-Yeah, does he know

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:50.367
that Daddy plays a serial killer
on television?

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.234
-We're gonna have to
break that one to him.

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:55.701
No, you know, there was recently
a day where I was like --

00:00:55.701 --> 00:00:57.200
I was doing something
really sweet with him,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.300
you know, like, in my lap.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.634
And then I sat on the remote.

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:03.934
And, like, you wouldn't think
this would --

00:01:03.934 --> 00:01:06.033
It just went right to Netflix
on the TV.

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.868
And my face was right on the TV.

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.601
And he was like, "Daddy!"

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:12.434
And I started to race around

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:14.300
because the next thing
he was gonna see --

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:16.467
-Was something crazy.
-Something really crazy.

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:19.767
So I was like...
And I got it off.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.167
-Yeah, you're like,
"Put on 'Bluey.'

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:22.501
Put on 'Bluey.'
'Bluey,' 'Bluey.'"

00:01:22.501 --> 00:01:24.267
-"Siri, Siri, Siri!"
-"Siri, Siri, put on --"

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:25.567
Sorry. No, yeah.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.434
By the way, can I say
how great you are on TikTok?

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.434
-Thank you.

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:30.567
-You went on --

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:32.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.467
You're crushing it.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:37.300
Right now I think you have
over 180 million views

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.701
on only 10 --

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:39.968
Higher? Yeah.

00:01:39.968 --> 00:01:41.367
Only 10 posts.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.467
-That sounds crazy to me, yes.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:46.968
That's -- That's like --
-That's a lot of views.

00:01:46.968 --> 00:01:49.968
-That's over a tenth
of a billion, isn't it?

00:01:49.968 --> 00:01:51.400
-It is.
-Isn't it?

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.901
-Yeah, of course.
-It's nearly 2/10,

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:55.701
which is nearly 1/5.

00:01:55.701 --> 00:01:58.501
And if we could round it up --
-Almost 3/10.

00:01:58.501 --> 00:01:59.801
-It's like a quarter.

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.434
-It's like you're doing
half a billion views.

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.167
-It's like half a --

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:06.667
-What made you like TikTok?
What made you get into --

00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.801
'Cause I would assume
maybe you go to Instagram.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:09.734
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:09.734 --> 00:02:11.501
Well, I mean, for me,

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:15.901
social media became a place of
a lot of anxiety over the years.

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.434
I started to use it
less and less and less.

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.634
-Yeah.

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:22.567
-And then, you know, I was
waiting for the right moment,

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:24.100
thinking maybe
I'll start a TikTok.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.367
Like, I wasn't sure.
I was on the fence.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:27.567
And then Taylor Swift
came out with her record.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:28.834
And --
-Yeah.

00:02:28.834 --> 00:02:30.734
"Anti-Hero" was the big one.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:32.801
-Yeah.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:37.267
And my podcast co-host
is a huge Swiftie,

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:38.634
like, a huge Swiftie.

00:02:38.634 --> 00:02:39.901
Shout-out to Nava.
She, like --

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:46.434
So we -- we made this --
this "Anti-Hero" thing,

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:47.434
this video thing.

00:02:47.434 --> 00:02:48.801
-Just 'cause
Taylor inspired you.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.133
-Yeah, for fun.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.601
And then when we made it,
we were like,

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:54.701
"I think that's the one
that I get on TikTok with."

00:02:54.701 --> 00:02:55.801
So, you know.
-Yeah.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.167
And then you did another one

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:59.701
with Meghan Trainor
"Made You Look" dance.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.434
-Only pop stars.
That's basically --

00:03:02.434 --> 00:03:04.534
-It shows --
I mean, you do enjoy dancing.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:07.434
When I think of you,
I think of singing and dancing.

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:08.767
-You do?
-Yeah.

00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:11.300
-[ Laughs ]
I do like to sing.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:14.300
I actually love to sing
and I love to dance.

00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:15.934
Music is my first passion
by far.

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:18.467
But I do not like
to mix them together.

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:20.601
Because usually
that's a musical.

00:03:20.601 --> 00:03:22.434
And I don't like musicals.
-That's not your thing.

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.567
But I do want to show a clip
of this "Made You Look" thing.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.734
It's very funny.
Here's Penn Badgley. Watch this.

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:28.234
-♪ I made you look ♪

00:03:28.234 --> 00:03:31.434
♪ Yeah, I look good
in my Versace dress ♪

00:03:31.434 --> 00:03:35.300
♪ But I'm hotter when
my morning hair's a mess ♪

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.133
♪ But even with my hoodie on ♪

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.934
♪ Bet I made you look ♪

00:03:39.934 --> 00:03:41.567
♪ I made you look ♪

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.534
-I mean, come on!

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:45.267
I would -- I love that.

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:48.534
-Yeah, it's fun.
It's fun. It is fun.

00:03:48.534 --> 00:03:51.300
-Bryan Cranston was just on
the show, and we were talking.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:52.868
And I heard this story

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:55.267
that you auditioned once
for "Breaking Bad."

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:59.934
-Yeah, actually, I mean, now
that it's become a little bit

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:04.534
