00:04:25.901 --> 00:04:27.100
You know what this is like.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.000
-I never made that it far
to test for something.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.300
But, yeah, I auditioned.
I auditioned for things, yeah.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:34.234
"Hi, Penn." You're like,
"Get out of my face, loser."

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.868
And I go, "Alright."
-Yeah, but this was like --

00:04:36.868 --> 00:04:39.868
It was the best script for
television that I'd ever read.

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.868
And actually, after
I didn't get it, I thought,

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:44.167
"Alright, great, that's fine,

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:47.167
but I don't know
if I can do any more TV."

00:04:47.167 --> 00:04:49.267
Like, that was the one.
-Really?

00:04:49.267 --> 00:04:52.100
-And I've been working
for nearly 20 years since

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.968
in television.
-Exactly, yeah.

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:57.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.701
You're crushing it with "You."

